<section class="container">
    <div class="row mt-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12 section-title">
        <div class="testimonial-heading">
          <h2 class="title">Types of Scholarships to Study Abroad</h2>
        </div>
        <span class="shape-line"><i class="icon-19"></i></span>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-5">
            <h4>Merit-Based Scholarships</h4>
            <p class="mt-3">Merit-based scholarships are awarded to students who have outstanding academic achievement. These scholarships are based solely on individual performance and accomplishments, rather than financial need or personal background. A student with high grades, leadership experience in school activities, or notable success in competitions may receive a merit-based scholarship that partially or fully covers tuition costs.</p>
    </div>
        <div class="mt-5">
            <h4>Student-Specific Scholarships</h4>
            <p class="mt-3">Student-specific scholarships are designed for individuals who meet certain demographic criteria, such as gender, ethnicity, religion, or nationality. These scholarships aim to provide access to education for groups who may be underrepresented or face specific challenges. A first-generation college student from a minority group may be eligible for a student-specific scholarship provided by organizations dedicated to promoting diversity in higher education.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-5">
            <h4>Need-Based Scholarships</h4>
            <p class="mt-3">
                Need-based scholarships are intended for students who require financial assistance to pursue their studies. These scholarships are awarded based on an assessment of financial need, often determined by a family’s income or other economic factors. The goal is to ensure that capable students can access education regardless of their financial situation. A student whose family income is insufficient to cover the costs of studying abroad may apply for a need-based scholarship. This support can cover expenses such as tuition, housing, or travel.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-5">
            <h4>Program-Based Scholarships</h4>
            <p class="mt-3">
                Program-based scholarships are linked to specific academic programs, fields of study, or exchange initiatives. These scholarships are offered by universities, academic departments, or partner organizations to encourage enrollment in targeted subject areas. A student planning to pursue a degree in computer science might qualify for a program-based scholarship offered by a university to support students in technology-related fields.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

